WEBVTT

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.020
Combat cyborgs.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:10.150
Research that greatly increased combat ability by allowing machines to fuse with a body.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:15.660
But due to many issues, including those of ethics and feasibility, the research was heavily criticized.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.360
So the research was stopped.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.000
And it was soon deemed that research of that sort was taboo.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.840
In the current case investigated by Riot Force 6,
combat cyborgs made an appearance.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.460
We’ve made a request for further help in the investigation.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:36.050
The Combat Cyborg Incident is one which holds a special meaning to my family.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.040
This is Ginga Nakajima with the 108th Battalion.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:33.670
Well then, before we practice this morning, there’s one thing I’d like to announce.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:40.290
Today, Sergeant Ginga Nakajima from the 108th Battalion will be temporarily stationed with Riot Force 6.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:40.840
Yes, ma’am.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.560
I’m Sergeant Ginga Nakajima from the 108th Battalion.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.270
I am honored to be working with you.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.980
The honor is ours.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.340
And one more.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.890
Nice to meet you.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:55.900
She’s been working on our captains’ Devices
for the past ten years,

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.850
and she’s the head of Precision Engineering, part of the Main Office’s Technical Department.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.360
I’m Mariel Atenza.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:07.500
She seems to have some business on the surface, so she’ll be staying with Riot Force 6 for a bit.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.360
It also looks like she’ll perform maintenance for your Devices.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:12.710
Call me anytime, okay?

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.950
Yes, ma’am.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.380
All right!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.010
Now that introductions are over,

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.850
shall we get going with this morning’s practice?

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:21.450
Yes, ma’am!

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.580
Lightning, gather here.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.430
Yes, ma’am!

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:28.000
Teana, you’re with me today.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:28.760
Yes, ma’am.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:31.850
Today is part six on how to decide
which attack pattern to use.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:32.900
Please go ahead.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.030
Ginga.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.070
Ma’am?

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:40.640
I want you to check up on Subaru’s skills a bit.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.390
Oh, yes, ma’am.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.120
A light mock battle, one-on-one.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.250
I want you to see how much Subaru’s grown.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.660
Yes, ma’am!

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.780
Storm Tooth

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:27.800
Protection

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:53.600
I see.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:54.980
Not bad.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:55.980
Agreed.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.180
Both of them are doing pretty well.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.990
<b>Revolver...</b>

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:10.910
Defenser

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.120
<b>...Cannon</b>

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:23.860
Buddy!

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.210
Gear 2nd

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:32.680
Wingroad

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.350
It’s almost like...

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:56.580
Subaru and Ginga

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.270
look like they’re having fun.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.210
It’s because Subaru loves her sister, right?

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:07.880
Ginga loves Subaru, as well.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:15.980
Subaru’s improved quite considerably.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:20.900
Ever since she joined, it’s because we’ve been monitoring her close-range combat basics.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:25.570
Nanoha and I have been bringing down the pain
on her every single damn day.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.490
At least that much.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:48.340
Okay! That’s it.

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:52.780
Subaru, you were close!

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.600
That’s great! You’ve gotten a lot better.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:03.520
I still have a long way to go.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.100
Your responses weren’t bad.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.110
So you lost in speed, eh?

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:11.900
Thank you, ma’am.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:13.640
During the last attack,

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:15.330
what would you have done, Erio?

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.770
Well, I guess...

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:21.750
Ginga, what did you think about Subaru’s growth?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.290
I was surprised.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.040
Our exchange of blows was rather smooth.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.550
The difference in her power is astounding.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:29.800
Did she pass?

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:30.880
Yes, ma’am!

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:31.890
By far.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:34.510
You’ll both be in the same unit for a while.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:36.070
So try your best together.

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:37.430
Yes, ma’am!

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.690
Okay, everyone, gather around.

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:41.350
Yes, ma’am!

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:46.520
It’s sudden, but why don’t we try a team battle with Ginga?

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.360
The five forwards against

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:53.160
a four-person team of the captains.

00:07:57.070 --> 00:08:00.860
You know Ginny, this happens from time to time.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:04.360
The captains will come at you quite seriously.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:08.370
First, you use your knowledge of the area
and illusionary magic to run from place to place,

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:13.780
and if by some chance you’re able to land a blow on them, they’re out.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:18.510
Ginga, you attack using your Device like Subaru, right?

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.850
The left knuckle is the one that attacks.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.440
Yes, ma’am.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:25.020
Then let’s go at it.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.440
Yes, ma’am!

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:54.130
Aina, I’m done!

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.490
Okay, you’ve done well.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.900
Wait just a second.

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:04.370
We have to make you really cute for when you go meet your mothers, don’t we?

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:06.860
Okay.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:09.180
We’ll end with this today.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.230
Everyone, release your protective clothing.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:12.650
Yes, ma’am.

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:16.020
You guys were close.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:17.870
If only you pushed a bit harder.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:23.070
We could have caused an upset if the last shift went well!

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:26.040
How frustrating!

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:27.950
I guess I wasn’t able to keep up.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:28.810
Sorry.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:29.620
No.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:31.750
Not at all, Ginga.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:36.210
Put together a report reflecting on
the battle while you’re still disappointed.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:37.680
Yes, ma’am.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.630
After you’ve rested a bit, let’s cool down and finish up.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.850
Good work.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.020
Thank you, ma’am!

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.480
Amazing!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.440
You guys do this every morning?

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:53.220
A battle with the captains, well, might be a bit special, but...

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:55.440
This is pretty normal for us.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:10:01.420
They need to push us right to our limits so that we’ll be okay if we’re deployed.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:03.120
It’s rather tough.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:09.030
And after practicing, we eat a lot,
rest up, and then we’re completely restored.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:10.000
I see.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:14.200
They all seem like nice kids.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.170
You mean Erio and everyone else,

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:18.240
or do you mean their Devices?

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:20.140
Both.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.390
Good morning.

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:31.390
Oh, uh... good morning.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:32.860
Morning, Vivio.

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:35.810
Excuse me.

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:38.200
Yeah, thank you.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.060
Don’t fall, all right?

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.030
Hey, Zafira!

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:44.160
It’s been a while.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.500
Shari, who’s that girl?

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.000
She’s...

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.250
Mama!

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.460
Vivio!

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:55.380
It’s dangerous.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.170
Don’t fall, okay?

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.250
Oh no!

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:03.380
It’s okay.

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:06.130
The ground is soft, and she fell cleanly.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:07.630
She’s not hurt.

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:09.350
That might be true, but...

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:13.270
Vivio, are you okay?

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:19.560
You’re not hurt, right?

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:22.360
Try your best to stand on your own.

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:24.330
Mama.

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:28.070
Mama Nanoha is right here for you.

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:35.200
Come on.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:38.410
Nanoha, you can’t. Vivio’s still small and all.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:44.000
Mama Fate.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.130
Be careful.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:52.900
If you got hurt, Vivio,
Mama Nanoha and Mama Fate would cry.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:55.140
I’m sorry.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:56.220
Geez.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:59.060
Mama Fate, you’re spoiling her a bit.

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:01.700
Mama Nanoha, you’re just too strict.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:04.660
Vivio, try your best next time, okay?

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:07.870
Something like that.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:12.000
Oh, in other words, she’s their chil—

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.920
Come on, Vivio.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.160
Vivio, your hair is cute.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.450
It’s Mama Nanoha’s ribbon.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:48.020
Aina did it for you, didn’t she?

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:48.660
Yep!

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:50.860
It’s nice, Vivio.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.540
I see. So she’s their foster child.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.380
Kind of like me.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.780
Nanoha is her legal guardian.

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:01.660
Fate is her godmother.

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.010
I see.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.490
Chew properly, okay?

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:18.150
Children sure do switch between crying and laughing in an instant.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.930
Subaru was like that too when she was a kid.

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:23.920
That’s...! Is that so?

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:25.610
Rein too.

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:29.780
Rein was an adult from the beginning.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.120
Liar.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:34.660
On the outside maybe,
but on the inside you were just like a baby.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:38.210
Aww... Hayate, that’s not true, is it?

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.190
I wonder.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.740
Vivio, that’s not good.
You can’t leave your green pepper there.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.050
I hate bitter things.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.850
They’re good!

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.540
If you don’t eat properly, you won’t get bigger.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:14:01.520
You know, if you’re too picky, you won’t become beautiful like your moms.

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:05.700
What are you going to do?

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:07.180
Eat.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:15.750
Sorry about this, but I’ll be borrowing Ginga and Subaru for a bit.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.630
Sure. Please look after them.

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:21.570
Subaru and Ginga will be going out
with Chief Engineer Mariel?

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:23.830
It’s their normal physical.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:26.170
At the Cranagan Medical Center.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:30.390
I think this should be all of them.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:33.390
Well, if we can’t find them
we’ll go out and look for them ourselves.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.890
Hurry up and go.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:36.690
Sorry about that.

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:37.300
Thanks.

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:38.680
Oh yeah, Subaru?

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:43.500
You know, those things you bought
for me when you had those medical exams?

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.900
Oh yeah, the Chocopods?

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:46.970
Yeah, that’s it.

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:51.530
I’ll pay as well, so buy some for the captains and the little ones.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:52.260
Roger.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.740
We’ve found no damaging information from the investigation into Riot Force 6.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.090
I see.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:08.810
There’s not much time before the Public Policy Convention.

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:12.200
We need to get harder evidence to use for the negotiations.

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:15.560
I’ll continue to have our investigation unit look into it.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:21.730
Even so, the Main Office’s investigation unit,
as well as a certain unit, seem to be investigating us.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:25.280
The usual, and you should deal with them as usual.

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:29.650
Within the Main Office’s inspection unit,
there is a troublesome officer with a rather Rare Skill.

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:34.120
If he gets serious, there’s a possibility that he might be able to dig up quite a bit.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:37.790
How despicable!

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:40.520
This is all necessary.

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:44.730
For everyone else to realize that, time and results are needed.

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:48.210
You won’t get support from the High Council?

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.370
I’ll ask them.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:52.970
How is Einherjar doing?

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:57.380
The final check on Unit 3 is running late,
but it’s proceeding smoothly.

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:58.960
Don’t fall behind!

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:01.560
Make it happen before the Convention.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.480
I have plans to do an investigation after this.

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:11.570
Einherjar, huh?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:12.970
What do you think?

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:13.940
Ma’am.

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:16.050
I believe it’s the hope of the surface world.

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:19.550
With that, we will be able to protect the safety and peace of the surface

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:24.960
without relying on anyone with Rare Skills
or the Main Office’s Dimensional Navy.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:27.150
That may be.

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:34.150
Whether it’s that other plan, or Einherjar, I can’t help but think they’re too powerful.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.960
Because it’s the path <i>he’s</i> chosen.

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:39.370
Yes, ma’am!

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.600
That’s the end of my report.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.760
The Church, as well as the senior staff

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:49.010
of the Main Office, seem to be plotting something.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:52.720
The Three Admirals? It should be fine to ignore them.

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.630
That’s right.

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:58.830
They no longer control anybody or the world.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:02.960
I shall leave the Convention to you.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.900
Do as you have up until now.

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:05.710
Roger.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:09.250
Yes, we can continue to act as we have.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:13.320
There will be no problems.

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:24.880
You two, I know you’ve been working hard lately,
but do you feel any discomfort anywhere?

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:26.340
None!

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:28.590
I’m feeling great!

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:29.820
Ditto.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:31.480
That’s great.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.780
In that case, let’s begin the periodic physical scan.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:41.640
Okay.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:57.420
Uno, you’re great.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:59.760
How’s your new body?

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:01.340
Of course, it’s nice.

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:04.680
It’s the result of your movement data, in the flesh.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.890
All of our little sisters are coming along nicely.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:10.060
Number VII, Sette.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:12.220
Number VIII, Otto.

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:14.400
Even Number XII, Deed.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:18.070
Their base and I.S. movements have been completed.

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:23.490
Number IX, Nove, and Number XI, Wendi, have their personal armaments completed.

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:27.700
Number II, Due, and Number V, Cinque,
are already running missions.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.170
A nice pace.

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:33.840
Our scrap-iron comrades have easily passed the planned production output.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:37.510
Were these called Gadget Drones?

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:40.710
That’s what the losers at the Bureau called them,

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:44.460
and I heard eventually the Doctor and Uno began calling them that.

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:46.390
How irresponsible.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:49.090
Who cares, it’s just a name.

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:51.690
Our names are just numbers too.

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:58.200
I like them quite a bit: our numbers and the names of our powers.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:18:59.650
How pointless.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:03.350
The day of the main event draws near.

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.990
I’m sure you guys are excited too.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:11.410
My weapons are finished...
I want some fights and explosions.

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:14.870
You guys have the most marvelous power.

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:17.340
Perfect for getting rowdy.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.790
You heard him.

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:20.970
Aren’t you excited, Nove?

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:21.950
Not really.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:26.520
I just have something I want to confirm.

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:29.790
Just what type of person our leader is.

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:35.900
Just if he really is someone proper to stand above us.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:43.780
Well, I don’t really understand. I guess it’ll come to me soon.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:45.780
That’s right.

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:53.730
While the preparations are finishing up,
why don’t we shoot off one rather large firework?

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:05.740
Without a doubt, this will be one hell of an event.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.510
Here you go. Sorry for making you wait.

00:20:15.510 --> 00:20:17.480
Thank you very much.

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:22.340
Oh yeah, and I’ll need three more ready-to-eat portions.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:24.410
Sure, I’ll bring those right out.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.760
Ginny, sorry for making you wait.

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:27.820
It’s okay.

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:30.480
You sure bought a bunch today, didn’t you?

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:32.580
Some for everyone.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.560
Ginny, say “ah.”

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:36.610
Here.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:43.200
It’s good.

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:51.270
But Subaru, you and Teana are so lively in Riot Force 6.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:52.910
It’s really nice.

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:57.480
Well, sometimes a lot happens, and it gets a bit tough.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.820
But I’m glad I got invited in.

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:05.870
Besides being with your best friend,
you get to be in the same unit as your hero.

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:09.280
Ginny, you’re my role model too, you know.

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:13.190
I want to get stronger and someday pass you.

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:17.200
You won’t be able to pass me that easily.

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:19.500
Because I’m going to get stronger too.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:21.480
Well, I’m trying my best.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:28.120
Subaru.

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:34.900
After this, we’re most likely going into battle with the combat cyborgs.

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:43.090
Let’s do our best.

00:21:43.930 --> 00:21:45.430
It’ll be okay.

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:49.470
We have the Revolver Knuckle our mother left behind for us,

00:21:49.470 --> 00:21:52.440
and right now we have our Calibers with us.

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:53.870
Calibers?

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.610
Mach and Blitz Calibers.

00:21:56.610 --> 00:21:59.800
Mach Caliber, this is your little sister, Blitz.

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:05.760
Sorry for making you wait.

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:10.310
Oh, Marie, would you like a Chocopod?

00:22:10.310 --> 00:22:11.820
Sure, I’ll take one!

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:16.060
It’s good!

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:17.310
Isn’t it?

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:18.060
Here you go.

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:19.020
Open up.

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:25.780
I received the latest prophecy interpretation from the Church today.

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:31.490
It seems the chance that the Public Policy Convention
will be targeted is rather high.

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:36.210
Of course, security will be as strict and good as ever.

00:22:36.210 --> 00:22:40.170
They’ll have Riot Force 6 protect the attendees.

00:22:40.170 --> 00:22:44.620
Really, it’d be great if we could all protect the perimeter,

00:22:44.620 --> 00:22:49.590
but it seems that only the three of us will be allowed to enter the building.

00:22:49.590 --> 00:22:55.050
Well, with the three of us together, we’ll figure something out.

00:22:55.050 --> 00:22:57.630
The front-line troops will do fine.

00:22:57.630 --> 00:22:59.770
We’ve trained them hard.

00:23:00.650 --> 00:23:04.530
The lieutenants are in as good a shape as ever.

00:23:04.530 --> 00:23:09.740
We’ll be raising everyone’s Device limiters to the third level tomorrow as well.

00:23:09.740 --> 00:23:14.660
If we can hold this place down,
I believe we’ll turn this situation around quickly.

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:19.210
It will definitely be all right.

00:25:17.530 --> 00:25:19.900
We head to protect Surface HQ,

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:22.400
and the members of Riot Force 6
see us off at the base.

00:25:22.400 --> 00:25:25.960
The attack comes silently at first, then abruptly.

00:25:33.030 --> 00:25:34.680
Take off!
